				</ukm:Metadata><Secondary><Body DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/body" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/body" NumberOfProvisions="132" RestrictExtent="N.I." RestrictStartDate="2022-10-26"><Part DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/part/I" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/part/I" NumberOfProvisions="5" ConfersPower="true" id="part-I" RestrictExtent="N.I." RestrictStartDate="2018-06-01"><Number>PART I</Number><Title>INTRODUCTORY</Title><P1group RestrictStartDate="2006-01-01"><Title>Meaning of “offence involving obligatory endorsement”</Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/article/3" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/article/3" id="article-3"><Pnumber>3</Pnumber><P1para><Text>For the purposes of this Order, an offence involves obligatory endorsement if it is an offence under a provision of the Road Traffic Orders specified in column 1 of Part I of Schedule 1 or an offence specified in column 1 of Part II of that Schedule and either—</Text><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/article/3/a" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/article/3/a" id="article-3-a"><Pnumber>a</Pnumber><P3para><Text>the word “obligatory” (without qualification) appears in column 6 (in the case of Part I) or column 3 (in the case of Part II) against the offence, or</Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/article/3/b" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/article/3/b" id="article-3-b"><Pnumber>b</Pnumber><P3para><Text>that word appears there qualified by conditions relating to the offence which are satisfied.</Text></P3para></P3></P1para></P1></P1group></Part></Body></Secondary></Legislation>